# CodeChecker skip list for kernel (device) code analysis.
# https://codechecker.readthedocs.io/en/latest/analyzer/user_guide/#skip
#
# Used with --drop-reports-from-skipped-files, so these paths are excluded from
# BOTH analysis and reporting. Unlike clang-tidy's HeaderFilterRegex this also
# suppresses clang-diagnostic-* findings, which is the point: the SFPI headers
# emit parse noise we cannot act on here.
#
# Exclusion-only by design. The translation units are the firmware wrappers
# (tt_metal/hw/firmware/src/.../{trisck,brisck,ncrisck,idle_erisck}.cc) with the
# kernel #included into them, so an allow-list keyed on kernels/ would skip
# every TU and analyze nothing. Anything not listed here is analyzed, which
# fails open for in-repo code as new device directories appear.

# Upstream toolchain: pinned SFPI release and the host libc/libstdc++ used for
# the analysis parse. Not fixable in this repo.
-/opt/tenstorrent/sfpi/*
-/usr/*

# Machine-generated JIT glue (chlkc_* headers and friends) emitted per compile
# into the kernel cache. Findings belong to the generator, not the output.
-*/tt-metal-cache/*
